    "text": "At the Cedar Deep mine, the following operational rules apply:\n\n* **Emergency Fan Activation:** The shift controller must activate emergency extraction fans whenever methane concentration exceeds `450 ppm`.\n* **Fan Speed Reduction:** If methane concentration remains below `450 ppm` and sensor array `GAS-R12` reports `stable`, the shift controller is permitted\u2014but not required\u2014to reduce fan speed.\n* **Seismic Activity and Evacuation:** If seismic activity exceeds `2.1 Ml`, the rescue team should evacuate Level 4 before any ventilation changes are made.\n* **Environmental Officer Permissions:** Environmental officers may view real-time gas readings on the Pithead Dashboard, but they must not modify fan parameters or override `GAS-R12` readings.",
